% layout 'bootstrap';
% title 'API help';

% content_for 'head' => begin
%= asset $_ for qw(swagger-ui.js swagger_init.js swagger-ui.css)
% end

<div>
    <h2><%= title %></h2>

    %= include 'layouts/info'

    <p>For developers, devops, and similar folks to get routes is easy. Call
    <code>script/openqa routes</code>. Even with matching regexes (with
    <code>-v</code> option).
    </p>

    <p><b>Hint:</b> Calling any non-existent route from your browser will show an
    error page with all available routes as help. E.g. try <%= link_to 'this
    link' => url_for('not_found') %>.
    </p>

    <h3>Swagger UI - Experimental</h3>
    <p>We also offer this experimental Swagger UI, which might be wrong or
    incomplete at this point. If you find a mistake, leave us a pull request
    :)</p>

    <div id="swagger-ui"></div>

</div>
